      "reason": "The question asks for Pacific, Atlantic and Indian basin results while excluding Southern and Arctic and folding marginal seas into parent oceans, so basin statistics depend on the stated partition and mask handling.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use the WOA23 basin mask via `select_basin`/`load_basin_mask`; report that WOA23 `basinmask_01` was used, with `include_marginal_seas=True`, and exclude Southern and Arctic Oceans from the Pacific/Atlantic/Indian basin summaries.",
        "Basin means must use the same basin mask definition for models and WOA23; marginal seas folded into parent oceans changes basin means, so state that choice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The analysis uses each model’s own volcello and asks for layer-volume percentages and a 200–1000 m average, so the meanings of tracer-cell volume and deriving layer thickness from volcello/areacello matter.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use each source's own `volcello` for 200–1000 m volume weighting and exceedance fractions; for CMIP6, `volcello` is the correct cell volume and already handles partial bottom cells.",
        "Do not derive layer thickness from `lev_bnds`; thickness/weights for any depth-range mean should come from `volcello` (or `cell_thickness_like` if thickness is needed)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
