      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The task needs volume-based statistics and also maps on a regular lon-lat grid, so integrals and percentages should be computed on native grids and regridding used only for display or pattern comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute every reported number on each source's own grid with its own weights; regrid only for Figure 2 display on a common lon-lat map, and say the maps are for display only.",
        "For the 200–1000 m layer statistics, do not vertically interpolate to other levels; integrate/average thickness-weighted on the original levels within that depth range."
