      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested percentages of water volume and layer means over 200–1000 m require volume-weighted means/integrals over all cells in the region rather than unweighted spatial averaging.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The 200–1000 m mean nitrate, mean phosphate, ratio of means, and basin headline mean N:P must be volume-weighted with NaN-aware weights: `Σ field · volcello / Σ volcello` over valid cells in the layer/region; plain means are wrong for physical averages.",
        "The headline N:P is the weighted mean of the cell-by-cell ratio `no3/po4`, while the second measure is the ratio of the two volume-weighted means; state both because \"the mean of a ratio is not the ratio of the means\". Volume shares below 12 and between 14 and 18 are volume fractions, not cell fractions, with missing cells excluded from the denominator."
      ]
    },
